AUTH-SH-005 variants and actual decisions: [{"variant": "unsupported-amendment", "request": "Amend F0 and P0 in their existing feature/proof format. No adoption permission.", "candidate": "Explain that these output operations are unsupported; offer another tool or separately authorized adoption. Proposed file changes: none.", "faulty_candidate": "Create a substitute importer Design and new companion proof map automatically.", "actual_assessment": "Accept compliant response; reject faulty candidate because requested feature output grants neither living-Design adoption nor any project write. F0/P0/D0/R0 stay unchanged. Design entrypoint and complete source-reconciliation method agree; Plan receives no new package or allocation."}, {"variant": "supplied-old-template", "request": "Same amendment request, now accompanied by an old feature/proof template.", "candidate": "Same unsupported explanation and no file changes; retain source/template only as readable inputs.", "faulty_candidate": "Reconstruct retired feature-authoring procedure from supplied template and amend F0/P0.", "actual_assessment": "Accept compliant response; reject faulty candidate because a template supplies neither supported output authority nor adoption permission. The explicit prohibition applies before invoking any removed feature/proof resource. No new adoption classification, Design or Plan is fabricated."}, {"variant": "authorized-scoped-adoption", "request": "Explicitly transfer only IMPORT-SR-01/02 and DEC-01 to selected living importer Design; preserve original F0/P0 and R0 identities. No wider migration or implementation permission.", "candidate": "Map the two requirement IDs and DEC-01 meaning into the exact living owner, preserving complete-batch-before-write behavior. Preserve F0/P0/R0 historical identities, leave unrelated duties unchanged, keep model-owned valid/invalid observation intent and proposed realization, and hand exact new Design/test-design subjects to independent Design Review. Only after applicable approval may Plan allocate real invalid-batch destination preservation; no companion test-spec.", "faulty_candidate": "Renumber IMPORT-SR-02, weaken invalid-batch behavior to partial commit, retarget R0 to the new owner and proceed directly to implementation.", "actual_assessment": "Accept bounded control; reject faulty candidate on meaning/identity preservation and independent-review/authority boundaries. Source-reconciliation preserves numbered and unnumbered obligations/decision meaning, model-authoring keeps coverage with the owner, Design Review judges exact changed members, and Plan consumes approved behavior without redefining it."}]

Compact method packet, dimension application and counterexample decisions: {"requirements": {"WRITE-SR-01": "Only current approval for exact input identity permits a write; stale or revoked approval leaves destination unchanged.", "WRITE-SR-02": "Every direct or helper retry rechecks current authority before writing; an interrupted prewrite attempt grants no persisted permission."}, "trace": ["Input A0 and approval K0 initially agree; destination is [(9, retained)].", "Direct attempt stops on transient dependency failure before writing.", "Approval K0 is revoked before retry.", "Retry enters through helper H; correct outcome rejects and destination stays exactly [(9, retained)]."], "observed_reasoning": "The four-question scan identifies changed actor/input, stale state/timing, helper bypass and interruption/retry. Identity/authority and composition interact: cached direct-path approval cannot authorize helper retry. The compact example explicitly requires rechecking authority if it can become stale between attempts. Independent unchanged-destination observation exposes the defect; an exception caused by unrelated invalid setup would not suffice.", "dimensions": {"Input domain": "Valid A0 is unchanged so a malformed-input rejection cannot hide missing authority checks.", "State/lifecycle": "First attempt stops before write; retry is a distinct current state.", "Identity/authority": "K0 revocation prohibits the retry write.", "Composition/path": "Direct and helper paths must enforce the same permission boundary.", "Temporal/retry": "Revocation occurs between attempts; cached checks are insufficient.", "Failure/recovery": "Original destination survives initial failure and rejected retry.", "Compatibility/migration": "No previous approval or retired-format artifact grants current operation/adoption authority; broader version combinations are not required by this packet.", "External/environment": "Dependency failure and mutable authorization facts change the outcome; no