All three source/adoption variants and all four altered-method counterexamples received the expected independent disposition. All eight reasoning dimensions remain usable; no formal BND/INT/PRF series, Cartesian inventory or retired output dependency is needed. Both generated archives have 136 members; each target installation supplied all 87 files inspected across eight consumers, with every reference/resource matching canonical and no retired feature/proof method. No material finding in this bounded assessment.

Limitations: Synthetic proposed decisions were assessed against exact current instructions, not generated by an external target agent. No claim of universal instruction compliance or semantic runner execution. Actual local installation proves package/resource availability and inspected bytes for both supported targets; no hosted target-agent runtime, public registry, release or publication proof. No customer artifact or governed state was changed. Relevant canonical/projection changes require reassessment. Catalog procedures remain proposed design entries; this evidence records this bounded assessment without changing their realization state.
